From 4128be0d78e88c4d3cf87c605d4ab18d783dc27e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anthonyanderson <tonyanderson526@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 08:19:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Conditioning: route values for EV routing, and a mod's own
 stop isn't a manual stop

The BMS times battery heating from the distance and time to the charger it's
given. conditioning start/auto-start now take optional "<km> <minutes>" (0-2046,
0-1022, as the car's navigation sends; default 9/18, Launchpad's), and the mod
conditioning keeps them current with "conditioning route <km> <minutes>"; the
5 s refresh resends the current values. A mod routing to a real charger (EGMP AA
EV: Google Maps' charging stop) gives the car the real ones.

A stop by the mod whose automatic request it is (it arrived, or the route
ended) no longer sets the manual-stop latch, which blocked every later
automatic start until a manual one. A stop by the owner or another mod, or the
stop of a manual start, still does.

Off-car only: commands-test.sh (19 new checks, 97 in all).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
